"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin the used size Chrome gives a replaced element whose size is NOT a
plain pixel pair: an `<svg>` that takes its ratio from `viewBox`, a
percentage width/height on svg/canvas/video, and an `em` width/height.
Before this change a viewBox was ignored (300/150 defaults), a percentage
axis collapsed to 1 px, and `height:1em` was read as `height:1px`.
Audience: browser-engine layout maintainers.

Chrome oracle (Chrome 159 headless shell, 900x760, `--dump-dom` of
getBoundingClientRect; page `<!doctype html>`,
`*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;font:16px/1.5 sans-serif}`, one parent
`<div>` at the top of `<body>` with the style shown, no whitespace between
siblings; VB is `viewBox="0 0 24 24"`):

| parent style            | fixture                                         | x   | y   | w   | h   |
|-------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|-----|-----|-----|-----|
| (none)                  | row A `<svg VB style="height:1em">`             | 0   | 32  | 16  | 16  |
| (none)                  | row A `<svg VB width=48>`                       | 16  | 0   | 48  | 48  |
| (none)                  | row A `<svg VB height=48>`                      | 64  | 0   | 48  | 48  |
| (none)                  | row A `<svg viewBox="0 0 200 50" style="width:100px">` | 112 | 23 | 100 | 25 |
| (none)                  | row B `<svg viewBox="0 0 200 50">`              | 0   | 0   | 900 | 225 |
| (none)                  | row C `<svg VB style="height:1em;border:2px solid red;padding:3px">` | 0 | 4 | 16 | 16 |
| (none)                  | row C `<svg VB width=48 height=20>`             | 16  | 0   | 48  | 20  |
| (none)                  | row C `<svg viewBox="0<TAB>0<LF>24 12" height=20>` | 64 | 0  | 40  | 20  |
| (none)                  | row C `<svg viewBox="0 0 0 24" height=20>`      | 104 | 0   | 300 | 20  |
| width:200px;height:100px| row D `<svg width="100%" height="100%">`        | 0   | 0   | 200 | 100 |
| width:200px;height:100px| row E `<canvas style="width:100%;height:100%">` | 0   | 0   | 200 | 100 |
| width:200px;height:100px| row F `<video style="width:50%;height:50%">`    | 0   | 0   | 100 | 50  |
| width:200px             | row G `<svg width="100%" height="100%">`        | 0   | 0   | 200 | 150 |
| width:400px;height:100px| row H `<svg width="50%">`                       | 0   | 0   | 200 | 150 |
| width:400px;height:100px| row H `<svg style="height:50%">`                | 0   | 157 | 300 | 50  |
| width:200px;height:100px| row I `<svg VB width="100%">`                   | 0   | 0   | 200 | 200 |
| (none)                  | row J `<div style="height:2em;width:10em">`     | 0   | 0   | 160 | 32  |
| (none)                  | row J `<div style="font-size:20px;height:1.5em">` | 0 | 32  | 900 | 30  |

Rules the table pins:
1. A valid viewBox (width and height > 0) gives the svg a ratio and NO size.
   One specified axis derives the other on the CONTENT box (row C: height
   16 px with 5 px border+padding per side is a 6x6 content box, 16x16
   border box); with neither axis specified the width is the available width
   (row B: 900) and the height follows. A zero-area viewBox is no viewBox.
2. The viewBox numbers may be separated by any whitespace (tab, newline).
3. A percentage width resolves against the container's content width, a
   percentage height against its DEFINITE content height; with an auto-height
   container the percentage height is `auto` (row G: 150).
4. `em` lengths in `width`/`height` are the element's own font-size.

Not asserted here: row H's second svg wraps in Chrome at y=157 (150 + 7 px
strut descent) and at 156 here -- the strut residue already filed in
doc/08_tracking/bug/web_replaced_media_residues_vs_chrome_159_2026-11-14.md --
so only its size is asserted.
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-REPLACED-005 — a replaced element resolves viewBox-ratio, percentage and em sizes like Chrome.
"""
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_foundation.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id
}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer_foundation.{parse_int}

val VW: i32 = 900
val VH: i32 = 760
val HEAD: text = "<html><head><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;font:16px/1.5 sans-serif}</style></head><body>"
val VB: text = "viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\""
val SIZED: text = "width:200px;height:100px"

val ROW_A: text = "<svg id=\"a\" " + VB + " style=\"height:1em\"></svg><svg id=\"c\" " + VB + " width=\"48\"></svg><svg id=\"d\" " + VB + " height=\"48\"></svg><svg id=\"e\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 50\" style=\"width:100px\"></svg>"
val ROW_B: text = "<svg id=\"b\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 50\"></svg>"
val ROW_C: text = "<svg id=\"g\" " + VB + " style=\"height:1em;border:2px solid red;padding:3px\"></svg><svg id=\"h\" " + VB + " width=\"48\" height=\"20\"></svg><svg id=\"i\" viewBox=\"0\t0\n24 12\" height=\"20\"></svg><svg id=\"j\" viewBox=\"0 0 0 24\" height=\"20\"></svg>"
val ROW_D: text = "<svg id=\"k\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></svg>"
val ROW_E: text = "<canvas id=\"l\" style=\"width:100%;height:100%\"></canvas>"
val ROW_F: text = "<video id=\"m\" style=\"width:50%;height:50%\"></video>"
val ROW_H: text = "<svg id=\"o\" width=\"50%\"></svg><svg id=\"q\" style=\"height:50%\"></svg>"
val ROW_I: text = "<svg id=\"r\" " + VB + " width=\"100%\"></svg>"
val ROW_J: text = "<div id=\"s\" style=\"height:2em;width:10em\"></div><div id=\"t\" style=\"font-size:20px;height:1.5em\"></div>"

fn probe(parent_style: text, inner: text, id: text, name: text) -> text:
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id(
        HEAD + "<div style=\"" + parent_style + "\">" + inner + "</div></body></html>", VW, VH, id, name)

fn box_of(parent_style: text, inner: text, id: text) -> text:
    probe(parent_style, inner, id, "x") + "," + probe(parent_style, inner, id, "y") + " " + probe(parent_style, inner, id, "w") + "x" + probe(parent_style, inner, id, "h")

fn size_of(parent_style: text, inner: text, id: text) -> text:
    probe(parent_style, inner, id, "w") + "x" + probe(parent_style, inner, id, "h")

describe "a replaced element resolves viewBox, percentage and em sizes like Chrome":
    it "AC-1: an svg with a viewBox and one specified axis takes the viewBox ratio":
        step("Chrome: height:1em is 16x16; width=48 is 48x48; height=48 is 48x48; 200x50 viewBox at width:100px is 100x25")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_A, "a")).to_equal("0,32 16x16")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_A, "c")).to_equal("16,0 48x48")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_A, "d")).to_equal("64,0 48x48")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_A, "e")).to_equal("112,23 100x25")

    it "AC-2: an svg with only a viewBox fills the available width":
        step("Chrome: viewBox 200x50 in a 900 px container is 900x225")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_B, "b")).to_equal("0,0 900x225")

    it "AC-3: the ratio applies to the content box under border-box sizing":
        step("Chrome: height 16 with 5 px border+padding per side is a 6x6 content box, 16x16 border box")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_C, "g")).to_equal("0,4 16x16")

    it "AC-4 (control): both axes specified ignore the viewBox ratio":
        step("Chrome: width=48 height=20 stays 48x20")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_C, "h")).to_equal("16,0 48x20")

    it "AC-5: viewBox numbers separated by tab and newline still give the ratio":
        step("Chrome: viewBox 24x12 at height=20 is 40x20")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_C, "i")).to_equal("64,0 40x20")

    it "AC-6 (control): a zero-area viewBox gives no ratio":
        step("Chrome: viewBox=\"0 0 0 24\" height=20 is the 300 px default wide")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_C, "j")).to_equal("104,0 300x20")

    it "AC-7: percentage width and height resolve against a sized container":
        step("Chrome: svg 100%/100% and canvas 100%/100% are 200x100; video 50%/50% is 100x50")
        expect(box_of(SIZED, ROW_D, "k")).to_equal("0,0 200x100")
        expect(box_of(SIZED, ROW_E, "l")).to_equal("0,0 200x100")
        expect(box_of(SIZED, ROW_F, "m")).to_equal("0,0 100x50")

    it "AC-8: a percentage height in an auto-height container is auto":
        step("Chrome: svg 100%/100% in a width:200px container is 200x150")
        expect(box_of("width:200px", ROW_D, "k")).to_equal("0,0 200x150")

    it "AC-9: one percentage axis leaves the other at its default":
        step("Chrome: width=50% of 400 is 200x150; height:50% of 100 is 300x50")
        expect(box_of("width:400px;height:100px", ROW_H, "o")).to_equal("0,0 200x150")
        expect(size_of("width:400px;height:100px", ROW_H, "q")).to_equal("300x50")

    it "AC-10: a percentage width feeds the viewBox ratio":
        step("Chrome: viewBox 24x24 at width=100% of 200 is 200x200")
        expect(box_of(SIZED, ROW_I, "r")).to_equal("0,0 200x200")

    it "AC-11: em widths and heights are the element's own font-size":
        step("Chrome: height:2em;width:10em at 16 px is 160x32; height:1.5em at font-size:20px is 30")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_J, "s")).to_equal("0,0 160x32")
        expect(box_of("", ROW_J, "t")).to_equal("0,32 900x30")

# Shrink-to-fit oracle (same Chrome 159 setup; each fixture is a direct child
# of `<body>`; sizes are `w x h`):
#
# | container                         | svg                | container w | svg     |
# |-----------------------------------|--------------------|-------------|---------|
# | `<div style="width:400px">`       | VB                 | 400         | 400x400 |
# | `<div style="display:inline-block">` | VB              | 0           | 0x0     |
# | `<button>`                        | VB                 | 16          | 0x0     |
# | `<div style="float:left">`        | VB                 | 0           | 0x0     |
# | `<div style="position:absolute">` | VB                 | 0           | 0x0     |
# | `<div style="display:flex">` + `<span>x</span>` | VB   | 900         | 892x892 |
# | `<div style="display:inline-block">` | VB height=48    | 48          | 48x48   |
# | `<button>`                        | VB height=48       | 64          | 48x48   |
# | `<div style="float:left">`        | VB height=48       | 48          | 48x48   |
# | `<div style="display:flex">` + `<span>x</span>` | VB height=48 | 900 | 48x48   |
# | `<div style="display:inline-block">` | (no viewBox)    | 300         | 300x150 |
#
# | `<div style="overflow:hidden">`   | VB float:left (the svg floats)    | - | 900x900 |
# | `<div style="position:relative;width:500px">` | VB position:absolute | - | 500x500 |
# | `<span>a` .. `b</span>` in body   | VB                 | 900         | 900x900 |
#
# A ratio-only svg contributes 0 to its container's min/max-content width and
# then fills whatever width the container resolved to.
#
# This engine floors every box width at 1 px (an EMPTY inline-block is 1x1
# here and 0x0 in Chrome), so the 0-wide rows are asserted as `<= Chrome + 1`
# and keep passing when the floor is removed. The floor is filed as residue
# 11 in doc/08_tracking/bug/web_replaced_media_residues_vs_chrome_159_2026-11-14.md.
#
# `display:inline-flex` is not supported: the box stays a full-width block
# (Chrome shrinks it, and the svg is 0 wide). BASE BEHAVIOUR RETAINED there --
# an unsized svg keeps the 300x150 default instead of filling 900 px. That is
# not the Chrome value; only the bound that guards the regression is asserted.
val STF_BLOCK: text = "<div id=\"p\" style=\"width:400px\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + "></svg></div>"
val STF_IB: text = "<div id=\"p\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + "></svg></div>"
val STF_BUTTON: text = "<div><button id=\"p\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + "></svg></button></div>"
val STF_FLOAT: text = "<div style=\"overflow:hidden\"><div id=\"p\" style=\"float:left\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + "></svg></div></div>"
val STF_ABS: text = "<div style=\"position:relative;height:60px\"><div id=\"p\" style=\"position:absolute\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + "></svg></div></div>"
val STF_FLEX: text = "<div id=\"p\" style=\"display:flex\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + "></svg><span>x</span></div>"
val STF_IB_H: text = "<div id=\"p\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " height=\"48\"></svg></div>"
val STF_BUTTON_H: text = "<div><button id=\"p\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " height=\"48\"></svg></button></div>"
val STF_FLOAT_H: text = "<div style=\"overflow:hidden\"><div id=\"p\" style=\"float:left\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " height=\"48\"></svg></div></div>"
val STF_FLEX_H: text = "<div id=\"p\" style=\"display:flex\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " height=\"48\"></svg><span>x</span></div>"
val STF_SVG_FLOAT: text = "<div id=\"p\" style=\"overflow:hidden\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " style=\"float:left\"></svg></div>"
val STF_SVG_ABS: text = "<div id=\"p\" style=\"position:relative;height:60px;width:500px\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " style=\"position:absolute\"></svg></div>"
val STF_SPAN: text = "<span id=\"p\">a<svg id=\"s\" " + VB + "></svg>b</span>"
val STF_INLINE_FLEX: text = "<div><div id=\"p\" style=\"display:inline-flex\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + "></svg></div></div>"
val STF_INLINE_FLEX_RULE: text = "<style>.x{display:inline-flex}</style><div><div id=\"p\" class=\"x\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + "></svg><span>hello</span></div></div>"
val STF_IB_PLAIN: text = "<div id=\"p\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><svg id=\"s\"></svg></div>"

fn page_probe(inner: text, id: text, name: text) -> text:
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id(HEAD + inner + "</body></html>", VW, VH, id, name)

fn stf(inner: text) -> text:
    "container " + page_probe(inner, "p", "w") + " svg " + page_probe(inner, "s", "w") + "x" + page_probe(inner, "s", "h")

fn px(inner: text, id: text, name: text) -> i32:
    val out = page_probe(inner, id, name)
    if out.len() == 0:
        return 100000
    parse_int(out)

describe "a ratio-only svg in a shrink-to-fit container":
    it "AC-12: contributes 0 intrinsic width to a shrink-to-fit container":
        step("Chrome: inline-block 0 wide with a 0x0 svg; asserted as <= Chrome + 1 (1 px box floor)")
        expect(px(STF_IB, "p", "w")).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        expect(px(STF_IB, "p", "w")).to_be_less_than(2)
        expect(px(STF_IB, "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(2)
        expect(px(STF_IB, "s", "h")).to_be_less_than(2)
        step("Chrome: button 16 wide with a 0x0 svg; asserted as <= 17")
        expect(px(STF_BUTTON, "p", "w")).to_be_greater_than(15)
        expect(px(STF_BUTTON, "p", "w")).to_be_less_than(18)
        expect(px(STF_BUTTON, "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(2)
        expect(px(STF_BUTTON, "s", "h")).to_be_less_than(2)
        step("Chrome: float:left div 0 wide with a 0x0 svg; asserted as <= 1")
        expect(px(STF_FLOAT, "p", "w")).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        expect(px(STF_FLOAT, "p", "w")).to_be_less_than(2)
        expect(px(STF_FLOAT, "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(2)
        expect(px(STF_FLOAT, "s", "h")).to_be_less_than(2)
        step("Chrome: position:absolute div 0 wide with a 0x0 svg; asserted as <= 1")
        expect(px(STF_ABS, "p", "w")).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        expect(px(STF_ABS, "p", "w")).to_be_less_than(2)
        expect(px(STF_ABS, "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(2)
        expect(px(STF_ABS, "s", "h")).to_be_less_than(2)

    it "AC-13: a specified height gives it an intrinsic width through the ratio":
        step("Chrome: height=48 makes the svg 48x48 and the container 48 (button 64)")
        expect(stf(STF_IB_H)).to_equal("container 48 svg 48x48")
        expect(stf(STF_BUTTON_H)).to_equal("container 64 svg 48x48")
        expect(stf(STF_FLOAT_H)).to_equal("container 48 svg 48x48")
        expect(stf(STF_FLEX_H)).to_equal("container 900 svg 48x48")

    it "AC-14: a definite available width is still filled":
        step("Chrome: 400 px block parent gives 400x400; a flex row beside a 8 px span gives 892x892")
        expect(stf(STF_BLOCK)).to_equal("container 400 svg 400x400")
        expect(stf(STF_FLEX)).to_equal("container 900 svg 892x892")

    it "AC-16: a floated, absolute or span-nested ratio-only svg fills its available width":
        step("Chrome: float in 900 px is 900x900; absolute in a 500 px block is 500x500; inside a span it is 900x900")
        expect(stf(STF_SVG_FLOAT)).to_equal("container 900 svg 900x900")
        expect(stf(STF_SVG_ABS)).to_equal("container 500 svg 500x500")
        expect(stf(STF_SPAN)).to_equal("container 900 svg 900x900")

    it "AC-17: an unsized svg in display:inline-flex does not fill the row":
        step("Base behaviour retained; Chrome 0: the svg must not be 900x900 (asserted: width <= 300)")
        expect(px(STF_INLINE_FLEX, "s", "w")).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        expect(px(STF_INLINE_FLEX, "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(301)
        expect(px(STF_INLINE_FLEX_RULE, "s", "w")).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        expect(px(STF_INLINE_FLEX_RULE, "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(301)

    it "AC-15: an svg without a viewBox keeps the 300x150 default":
        step("Chrome: inline-block around a plain svg is 300 wide")
        expect(stf(STF_IB_PLAIN)).to_equal("container 300 svg 300x150")

# Constrained or out-of-flow ratio-only svg inside a span (Chrome 159; `a` and
# `b` are 8.9 px each there and 9 px here; `<span id="n">next</span>` follows):
#
# | svg style                         | svg     | span w | next x |
# |-----------------------------------|---------|--------|--------|
# | `max-width:24px`                  | 24x24   | 41.8   | 41.8   |
# | `min-width:40px;max-width:40px`   | 40x40   | 57.8   | 57.8   |
# | `max-width:24px`, in a nested span| 24x24   | 41.8   | 71.8 (after a 30 px float row above) |
# | `position:absolute`               | 891x891 | 17.8   | 17.8   |
# | `float:left;max-width:30px`       | 30x30   | 17.8   | 47.8   |
#
# Only an in-flow svg widens the span, and only by its constrained width.
# The out-of-flow svg itself is sized against its containing block, never the
# span: absolute -> 891x891 (900 minus its 8.9 px static position), float ->
# 30x30. `<canvas style="position:absolute">` / `<video style="float:left">`
# in a span are 300x150 and leave the span 17.8 wide.
fn span_row(svg_style: text) -> text:
    "<div style=\"position:relative\"><span id=\"p\">a<svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " style=\"" + svg_style + "\"></svg>b</span><span id=\"n\">next</span></div>"

val SPAN_NESTED: text = "<div><span id=\"p\">a<span id=\"q\"><svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " style=\"max-width:24px\"></svg></span>b</span><span id=\"n\">next</span></div>"

# Extreme ratios (Chrome 159, `width=100` unless noted):
#
# | viewBox w x h              | Chrome        |
# |----------------------------|---------------|
# | 1000000 x 0.001 (height=100) | 33554432x100 |
# | 1 x 10000000000            | 100x33554432  |
# | 1 x 10000000               | 100x33554432  |
# | 0.1 x 1000000              | 100x33554432  |
# | 0.001 x 100                | 100x9999900   |
# | 0.0001 x 100               | 100x33554432  |
# | 0.01 x 1000000             | 100x150 (measured 150 or 152 by page) |
# | 0.001 x 1000000            | 100x150       |
# | 0.001 x 1000000, no size   | 300x150       |
# | 0.001 x 10000              | 100x152       |
# | 0.00001 x 100              | 100x152       |
#
# Derived sizes saturate at 33554432. A viewBox under one unit wide whose
# height is more than 10^7 times its width gives no ratio (plain defaults).
# At exactly 10^7 Chrome is not consistent (0.1 x 1000000 keeps the ratio,
# 0.001 x 10000 drops it), so no row is asserted on that boundary.
val MAX_PX: i32 = 33554432
val RATIO_WIDE: text = "<div id=\"p\"><svg id=\"s\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000000 0.001\" height=\"100\"></svg></div>"
val RATIO_TALL: text = "<div id=\"p\"><svg id=\"s\" viewBox=\"0 0 0.001 1000000\" width=\"100\"></svg></div>"
val RATIO_EXP: text = "<div><svg id=\"s\" viewBox=\"0 0 1e30 1e-30\" height=\"100\"></svg></div>"

describe "a constrained or out-of-flow ratio-only svg inside a span":
    it "AC-18: max-width and min-width bound the span's width":
        step("Chrome: max-width:24px gives a 24x24 svg, span 41.8, next at 41.8 (here 42)")
        expect(stf(span_row("max-width:24px"))).to_equal("container 42 svg 24x24")
        expect(px(span_row("max-width:24px"), "n", "x")).to_equal(42)
        step("Chrome: min-width:40px;max-width:40px gives 40x40, span 57.8 (here 58)")
        expect(stf(span_row("min-width:40px;max-width:40px"))).to_equal("container 58 svg 40x40")
        expect(px(span_row("min-width:40px;max-width:40px"), "n", "x")).to_equal(58)
        step("Chrome: the same svg one span deeper gives the same 41.8 span")
        expect(stf(SPAN_NESTED)).to_equal("container 42 svg 24x24")
        expect(px(SPAN_NESTED, "q", "w")).to_equal(24)

    it "AC-19: an out-of-flow svg does not widen the span":
        step("Chrome: position:absolute leaves the span 17.8 wide and next at 17.8; asserted 17 < v < 20 (1 px box floor)")
        expect(px(span_row("position:absolute"), "p", "w")).to_be_greater_than(17)
        expect(px(span_row("position:absolute"), "p", "w")).to_be_less_than(20)
        expect(px(span_row("position:absolute"), "n", "x")).to_be_greater_than(17)
        expect(px(span_row("position:absolute"), "n", "x")).to_be_less_than(20)
        step("Chrome: float:left;max-width:30px leaves the span 17.8 wide; asserted 17 < w < 20")
        expect(px(span_row("float:left;max-width:30px"), "p", "w")).to_be_greater_than(17)
        expect(px(span_row("float:left;max-width:30px"), "p", "w")).to_be_less_than(20)

    it "AC-22: an out-of-flow replaced box in a span is sized against its containing block":
        step("Chrome: the absolute svg is 891.1x891.1 (asserted 890 < v < 893)")
        expect(px(span_row("position:absolute"), "s", "w")).to_be_greater_than(890)
        expect(px(span_row("position:absolute"), "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(893)
        expect(px(span_row("position:absolute"), "s", "h")).to_be_greater_than(890)
        expect(px(span_row("position:absolute"), "s", "h")).to_be_less_than(893)
        step("Chrome: the float:left;max-width:30px svg is 30x30")
        expect(px(span_row("float:left;max-width:30px"), "s", "w")).to_equal(30)
        expect(px(span_row("float:left;max-width:30px"), "s", "h")).to_equal(30)
        step("Chrome: an absolute canvas in a span is 300x150 and the span stays 17.8 wide (asserted 17 < w < 20)")
        expect(stf("<div id=\"p\" style=\"position:relative;height:160px\"><span id=\"q\">a<canvas id=\"s\" style=\"position:absolute\"></canvas>b</span></div>")).to_equal("container 900 svg 300x150")
        expect(px("<div id=\"p\" style=\"position:relative;height:160px\"><span id=\"q\">a<canvas id=\"s\" style=\"position:absolute\"></canvas>b</span></div>", "q", "w")).to_be_greater_than(17)
        expect(px("<div id=\"p\" style=\"position:relative;height:160px\"><span id=\"q\">a<canvas id=\"s\" style=\"position:absolute\"></canvas>b</span></div>", "q", "w")).to_be_less_than(20)
        step("Chrome: a floated video in a span is 300x150 and the span stays 17.8 wide")
        expect(stf("<div id=\"p\" style=\"overflow:hidden\"><span id=\"q\">a<video id=\"s\" style=\"float:left\"></video>b</span></div>")).to_equal("container 900 svg 300x150")
        expect(px("<div id=\"p\" style=\"overflow:hidden\"><span id=\"q\">a<video id=\"s\" style=\"float:left\"></video>b</span></div>", "q", "w")).to_be_greater_than(17)
        expect(px("<div id=\"p\" style=\"overflow:hidden\"><span id=\"q\">a<video id=\"s\" style=\"float:left\"></video>b</span></div>", "q", "w")).to_be_less_than(20)

describe "an extreme viewBox ratio is bounded":
    it "AC-20: the derived axis stops at the largest layout size":
        step("Chrome: viewBox 1000000 x 0.001 at height=100 is 33554432x100")
        expect(stf(RATIO_WIDE)).to_equal("container 900 svg 33554432x100")
        step("Chrome: a tall viewBox at least one unit wide saturates too: 1 x 10000000000 at width=100 is 100x33554432")
        expect(stf("<div id=\"p\"><svg id=\"s\" viewBox=\"0 0 1 10000000000\" width=\"100\"></svg></div>")).to_equal("container 900 svg 100x33554432")

    it "AC-23: a viewBox under one unit wide and over 10^7 times taller gives no ratio":
        step("Chrome: viewBox 0.001 x 1000000 at width=100 is 100x150, and 300x150 with no size")
        expect(stf(RATIO_TALL)).to_equal("container 900 svg 100x150")
        expect(stf("<div id=\"p\"><svg id=\"s\" viewBox=\"0 0 0.001 1000000\"></svg></div>")).to_equal("container 900 svg 300x150")
        step("Chrome: viewBox 0.01 x 1000000 at width=100 is 100x150")
        expect(stf("<div id=\"p\"><svg id=\"s\" viewBox=\"0 0 0.01 1000000\" width=\"100\"></svg></div>")).to_equal("container 900 svg 100x150")
        step("Chrome: viewBox 0.001 x 100 (10^5 times taller) keeps its ratio: 100x9999900; asserted 9999000 < h < 10001000")
        expect(px("<div><svg id=\"s\" viewBox=\"0 0 0.001 100\" width=\"100\"></svg></div>", "s", "h")).to_be_greater_than(9999000)
        expect(px("<div><svg id=\"s\" viewBox=\"0 0 0.001 100\" width=\"100\"></svg></div>", "s", "h")).to_be_less_than(10001000)

    it "AC-24: a malformed viewBox never crashes":
        step("Malformed exponent viewBox does not crash and stays bounded")
        expect(px(RATIO_EXP, "s", "w")).to_be_greater_than(0)
        expect(px(RATIO_EXP, "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(MAX_PX + 1)

describe "a floated or absolute canvas and video keep their default box":
    it "AC-21: 300x150 in each position (Chrome 159)":
        step("Chrome: float:left canvas and video are 300x150")
        expect(stf("<div id=\"p\" style=\"overflow:hidden\"><canvas id=\"s\" style=\"float:left\"></canvas></div>")).to_equal("container 900 svg 300x150")
        expect(stf("<div id=\"p\" style=\"overflow:hidden\"><video id=\"s\" style=\"float:left\"></video></div>")).to_equal("container 900 svg 300x150")
        step("Chrome: position:absolute canvas and video in a 500 px block are 300x150; left:310px is honoured")
        expect(stf("<div id=\"p\" style=\"position:relative;height:160px;width:500px\"><canvas id=\"s\" style=\"position:absolute\"></canvas></div>")).to_equal("container 500 svg 300x150")
        expect(stf("<div id=\"p\" style=\"position:relative;height:160px;width:500px\"><video id=\"s\" style=\"position:absolute;left:310px\"></video></div>")).to_equal("container 500 svg 300x150")
        expect(px("<div id=\"p\" style=\"position:relative;height:160px;width:500px\"><video id=\"s\" style=\"position:absolute;left:310px\"></video></div>", "s", "x")).to_equal(310)

# Absolute replaced box in a span, insets and positioned spans (Chrome 159;
# `S` = `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="position:absolute;...">`):
#
# | fixture                                                              | svg x | svg     |
# |----------------------------------------------------------------------|-------|---------|
# | `<div style="width:600px"><span style="position:relative">a S</span>` | 8.9   | 0x0     |
# | same, span text `abcdef` (48 wide), `left:0`                         | 0     | 48x48   |
# | same, `left:2px;width:50%`                                           | 2     | 24x24   |
# | `<div style="position:relative;width:200px">some text <span>a S`, `left:1px` | 1 | 199x199 |
# | same, `right:1px`                                                    | 0     | 199x199 |
# | same with `height:50px` on the div, `left:10px;height:50%`           | 10    | 25x25   |
# | same, `<canvas style="position:absolute;left:1px;width:50%">`        | 1     | 100x50  |
#
# The containing block is the nearest POSITIONED ancestor, a span included
# (its box); an inset is measured from that block's edge and leaves the rest
# of its width available. The canvas height (Chrome keeps the 2:1 ratio: 50)
# is 150 here and is not asserted.
fn abs_in_positioned_span(text_run: text, svg_style: text) -> text:
    "<div style=\"width:600px\"><span id=\"p\" style=\"position:relative\">" + text_run + "<svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " style=\"position:absolute;" + svg_style + "\"></svg></span></div>"

fn abs_in_span_of(div_style: text, child: text) -> text:
    "<div id=\"p\" style=\"position:relative;width:200px;" + div_style + "\">some text <span>a" + child + "</span></div>"

fn abs_svg(svg_style: text) -> text:
    "<svg id=\"s\" " + VB + " style=\"position:absolute;" + svg_style + "\"></svg>"

describe "an absolute replaced box in a span uses the nearest positioned ancestor":
    it "AC-25: a positioned span is the containing block":
        step("Chrome: static position at the span's right edge leaves 0 available: 0x0 (asserted w < 2)")
        expect(px(abs_in_positioned_span("a", ""), "s", "w")).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        expect(px(abs_in_positioned_span("a", ""), "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(2)
        step("Chrome: left:0 in a 48 px span is 48x48 at x=0 (asserted 47 < w < 50)")
        expect(px(abs_in_positioned_span("abcdef", "left:0"), "s", "x")).to_equal(0)
        expect(px(abs_in_positioned_span("abcdef", "left:0"), "s", "w")).to_be_greater_than(47)
        expect(px(abs_in_positioned_span("abcdef", "left:0"), "s", "w")).to_be_less_than(50)
        step("Chrome: left:2px;width:50% of the 48 px span is 24x24 at x=2")
        expect(px(abs_in_positioned_span("abcdef", "left:2px;width:50%"), "s", "x")).to_equal(2)
        expect(px(abs_in_positioned_span("abcdef", "left:2px;width:50%"), "s", "w")).to_equal(24)
        expect(px(abs_in_positioned_span("abcdef", "left:2px;width:50%"), "s", "h")).to_equal(24)

    it "AC-26: an inset is measured from the containing block, not the span":
        step("Chrome: left:1px in a 200 px positioned div is 199x199 at x=1")
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("", abs_svg("left:1px")), "s", "x")).to_equal(1)
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("", abs_svg("left:1px")), "s", "w")).to_equal(199)
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("", abs_svg("left:1px")), "s", "h")).to_equal(199)
        step("Chrome: right:1px is 199x199 at x=0")
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("", abs_svg("right:1px")), "s", "x")).to_equal(0)
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("", abs_svg("right:1px")), "s", "w")).to_equal(199)
        step("Chrome: left:10px;height:50% of a 50 px div is 25x25 at x=10")
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("height:50px", abs_svg("left:10px;height:50%")), "s", "x")).to_equal(10)
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("height:50px", abs_svg("left:10px;height:50%")), "s", "w")).to_equal(25)
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("height:50px", abs_svg("left:10px;height:50%")), "s", "h")).to_equal(25)
        step("Chrome: canvas left:1px;width:50% is 100 wide at x=1")
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("", "<canvas id=\"s\" style=\"position:absolute;left:1px;width:50%\"></canvas>"), "s", "x")).to_equal(1)
        expect(px(abs_in_span_of("", "<canvas id=\"s\" style=\"position:absolute;left:1px;width:50%\"></canvas>"), "s", "w")).to_equal(100)
